    "title": "Nebraska Secretary of State certifies two new political parties - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Chase Foix Maren Ewertz ,\n1 days ago\nNEBRASKA ( KCAU ) — Two new Nebraska political parties are one step closer to having candidates on the November election ballot.\nA ruling from the Nebraska Supreme Court on Wednesday now allows for the establishment of the Nebraska Working People Party and the America First Party.\nNebraskans can immediately begin registering with either new political party. A newly updated voter registration form can be found by clicking here .\nStory continues below\nNominations for the general election will be accepted. To qualify, candidates must meet several requirements at the time of filing.\nThose requirements include being nominated by a state convention of the political party, as well as submitting a nomination petition signed by 25 registered voters of the party in the appropriate jurisdiction.\nAll materials must be submitted by 5 p.m. on September 1.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KCAU 9 News | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
    "summary": "By Chase Foix Maren Ewertz , NEBRASKA ( KCAU ) — Two new Nebraska political parties are one step closer to having candidates on the November election ballot. Nebraskans can immediately begin registering with either new political party. A newly updated voter registration form can be found by clicking here . To qualify, candidates must meet several requirements at the time of filing. Those requirements include being nominated by a state convention of the political party, as well as submitting a nomination petition signed by 25 registered voters of the party in the appropriate jurisdiction.",
